{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-from-epsilon","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-from-epsilon","kind":"definition","title":"The substrate parameter $q$ as $1 + \\varepsilon$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-reeb-epsilon"],"tags":["substrate-parameter","surreal","categorical-primitive","q-expansion","classical-limit"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QFromEpsilon","text":"q-from-epsilon.md","leanSource":"q-from-epsilon.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:q-from-epsilon\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>The substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1 + \\varepsilon</code></em></p>\n<p>With the Reeb infinitesimal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varepsilon \\in \\mathrm{Der}(A)</code> in hand (<a href=\"#def:reeb-epsilon\">Reeb infinitesimal</a>), the substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> is now a derived quantity.</p>\n<p><strong>Definition.</strong> The <strong>substrate parameter associated to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varepsilon</code></strong> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">q := 1 + \\varepsilon,</code></pre>\n<p>interpreted inside the ordered field generated by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varepsilon</code> over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{R}</code>.</p>\n"}
